<http://www.spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/event/80601AKMRNLTTLLDPKKJNNMTCGCVKGPLC>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Stand-Up and Deliver at The Improv Centre";
  schema:description """
	<h2>Stand-Up is BACK at The Improv Centre!</h2><span><br/></span>Get ready for four comedians and one hilarious night of stand-up on Granville Island!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Stand-up comedy returns to The Improv Centre with <span class=\"ItalicText\">Stand-Up and Deliver</span>, hosted and curated by Vancouver comedian Arya Afshar. Headliner Katie-Ellen Humphries is joined by Aaron Read, Rachel Schaefer, and Susan Grossman for an evening of stand-up at TIC.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">HOST</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://[https://vancouverguardian.com/vancouver-comedian-arya-afshar/\">Arya Afshar</a> is a Vancouver comedian whose sets balance social commentary with silly observations about everyday life. He brings a sharp point of view to the stage, with comedy that aims to make audiences think while they laugh.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">HEADLINER</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://[https://www.katie-ellen.com/\">Katie-Ellen Humphries</a> is a Vancouver-based stand-up comedian, writer, and sketch performer. A founding member of The Lady Show and a veteran of the award-winning comedy cabaret Atomic Vaudeville, Katie-Ellen is also a regular on CBC Radio’s <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Debaters</span>, where she has worked as a writer and Associate Producer.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Aaron Read</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://[https://thesonarnetwork.com/people/aaron-read/\">Aaron Read</a> is an award-winning stand-up comedian, improviser, actor, and visual artist from Vancouver. His comedy moves between silliness and sad-psychedelia, and his credits include CBC Gem’s <span class=\"ItalicText\">The New Wave of Stand Up</span> and Just For Laughs’ New Faces of Comedy showcase.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Rachel Schaefer</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://[https://vancouverguardian.com/chatting-with-vancouver-comedian-rachel-schaefer/\">Rachel Schaefer</a> is a Vancouver comedian known for personal stories, everyday observations, and a willingness to poke fun at herself. She has been featured on Just For Laughs, CBC Gem’s <span class=\"ItalicText\">The New Wave of Standup</span>, and SiriusXM Comedy Club.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Susan Grossman</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://[https://www.instagram.com/susangrossmancomedy/\">Susan Grossman</a> is a queer, faceblind Gen X-er doing observational comedy about aging, bureaucracy, and online dating – where every first date might also be a second date. They write text messages like a 19th century literary icon and are ready with hot takes on emoji responses. Come laugh at Susan.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-01T19:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/improvcentrevancouver/files/e317efa9-ed5c-437c-a32e-446226008088.jpg>;
